SCOPE OF THE ABOVE

The MIT licence above covers only what the 1.6 port added, which here is a
small part of the shipped files:

  - the editing of the six patch files: seven dead targets removed, one
    followed into Vanilla Factions Expanded - Medieval 2, one operation that
    had never matched anything removed, two comments corrected, the files
    renamed after the mod each one targets
  - the packaging and the documentation

There is no assembly and no source code in this mod. It is XML only.

IT DOES NOT COVER THE ORIGINAL MOD, AND THE ORIGINAL MOD IS MOST OF WHAT IS
HERE. The choice of buildings to patch and every particle value on them - the
sizes, the fleck defs, the per-rotation offsets, which buildings smoke only
while a bill is running - are MysticFelines':

  https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2819074837

Not one of those numbers was retuned. Three operations gained one field, an
indoorAlt of Owl_SmokeIndoors - on the darklight hearth, the dark firepit and
the wood-fired crematorium - which applies MysticFelines' own rule to the three
places she had applied it inconsistently. No value was altered anywhere.

The whole of this mod is that judgement; the port is only the work of finding
out which of those buildings still exist in 1.6.

They never declared a licence for it, so none is granted here and none can be.
It is redistributed under the usual practice for abandoned mods - explicit
credit, a link to the original, and removal on request.

If MysticFelines asks for this to be taken down, it comes down. Immediately,
and without discussion.

ATTRIBUTION.md records what was taken and what was changed.
